0Biological Species in Pleurotus.RONALD H. PETERSEN, KAREN W. HUGHES, AND NADEZHDA PSURTSEVA///Keys abound for limited groups (Vilgalys et al., 1993, for the P. ostreatus complex) or of limited accuracy (Pilát, 1935; Kühner and Romagnesi, 1953; Hilber, 1982, 1993, 1997).///To devise a key to this group is fraught with problems, for basidiome colors, hosts, and stature often intergrade, and geographical distribution is often wide and therefore creates overlaps. ///Especially vexing is the separation of Pleurotus pulmonarius from its sister monomitic, pleurotoid species, P. ostreatus and P. populinus./// With these problems in mind, the following key to biological species is offered.020134324200
